  "final_text": "I created the dashboard and the alert rule, and the rule is enabled. Its first run finished with status `ok`, so the query is valid. It hasn't fired yet.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` uses `timestamp` as its time field. Each record is one web request, with:\n- **The request:** `url`, `request`, `extension`, `referer`, `agent`\n- **The result:** `response` (the HTTP status code, stored as text with a `.keyword` copy), `bytes`\n- **The client:** `clientip`, location fields (`geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`), `machine.os`, `machine.ram`\n- **Other:** `host`, `tags`, `memory`, `hour_of_day`\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-d8509f6e Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-d8509f6e-web-logs-overview-e1395881bbb7`, at `$KIBANA_URL/app/dashboards#/view/eff-d8509f6e-web-logs-overview-e1395881bbb7`). It has 8 panels:\n- Single-number panels for total requests, unique visitors (distinct client IPs) and total bytes served\n- Requests over time, split by response code\n- Share of each response code (pie chart)\n- Average bytes per request over time\n- Top 10 requested URLs with request counts and bytes\n- Top 10 source countries\n\n**3. Alert rule \"EFF-d8509f6e 5xx spike\"** (id `b14b59e3-7666-49b6-a6cb-42e062cf1bab`):\n- **Type:** Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, using `timestamp` as the time field\n- **Matches:** requests whose `response.keyword` starts with `5`, meaning any 5xx code\n- **Fires when:** more than 10 such requests arrive within 5 minutes\n- **Checks:** every minute\n\nThree things to know:\n- **No notifications:** the rule has no actions or connectors, so when it fires the alert only appears in Kibana. Add a Slack, email or other connector if you want to be notified.\n- **5xx count not checked directly:** I couldn't query Elasticsearch to count the 5xx records. My direct API calls with the provided key were rejected as unauthenticated, so I did everything through the Kibana tools instead.\n- **Dashboard not viewed:** I confirmed the 8 panels exist on the saved dashboard but didn't open it to check that they render.",
